      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. For the CLI Parser: In  post-sync.py \u0027s  direct_main  function, the  --sync-duration-seconds  argument was previously hardcoded as  type\u003dint . I have updated it to  type\u003dfloat  so   \n  that it safely accepts and preserves decimal values when running hooks manually outside of  repo .\n  2. For the Placeholder ( REPO_SYNC_DURATION ): Python\u0027s native  str()  function automatically handles floating-point numbers correctly (e.g.,  str(12.345)  becomes  \"12.345\" ). Since we\n  populate the environment variable using  str(sync_duration_seconds)  before expanding placeholders, the  ${REPO_SYNC_DURATION}  token will correctly evaluate to the full float string   \n  without any truncation.",
